### Page 1 of 3

```text
FINANCE COMMITTEE
MINUTES
A meeting of the Finance Committee was held on Tuesday, February 3, 2026, in City Council
Chambers and via electronic meeting, starting at 12:00 p.m. Those in attendance were as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS: Ken Esquibel, Chairman; Mark Moody; Jeff White; and Lawrence
Wolfe.
AGENDA ITEMS
18.
LEASES/CONTRACTS/LEGAL:
c)
Lease Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and the Girl Scouts of Montana
and Wyoming, for 45.93 acres of city-owned real property located near the former
Roundtop Water Treatment Facility to be used for the purposes of conducting
activities consistent with the By-Laws and Articles of Incorporation of the Girl
Scouts of Montana and Wyoming. (Revenue to the City)
Mr. Moody moved to approve in an amount of $100.00 annually for the period of 5 years, seconded
by Mr. Wolfe. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Jason Sanchez, Community Recreation & Events Director, provided a staff report. Committee
member Wolfe commented on the item.
19.
CONTRACT MODIFICATIONS:
a)
Contract Modification #1 to Contract #8111 between the City of Cheyenne, Office
of Youth Alternatives, and the Laramie County Community Juvenile Services Joint
Powers Board for a Juvenile Diversion Coordinator to provide diversion related
services to increase the potential contract dollar amount, (Revenue to the City)
Mr. Moody moved to approve in an amount of $78,175.65, seconded by Mr. Wolfe. Motion carried
by unanimous voice vote.
Jay Sullivan, Youth Alternatives Director, provided a staff report.
20.
CONSIDERATION OF BIDS/PURChASES/REQUESTS FOR PROPOSALS:
b)
Consideration of Bid #S-8-26 for an Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and
Fencetrak, Inc. dlb/a Full Tilt Services, for the Dry Creek Restoration Project.
Phase
1: Meadowland, Holmes, and Henderson Ditches project. (2023-2026
Optional 1% Sales Tax Fund)
```

### Page 2 of 3

```text
Mr. Moody moved to accept the bid in an amount not to exceed $458,282.50, seconded by Mr.
Wolfe. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Sam Berta, Engineering, provided a staff report. Chainuan Esquibel and all committee members
commented on the item.
c)
Consideration of Bid #S- 10-26 for an Agreement between the City of Cheyenne
and f’ieehanica1 Systems, Inc., for the North Cheyenne Community Park Drainage
Improvement project. (Development Impact Fees)
Mr. Wolfe moved to accept the bid in an amount not to exceed $121,606.00, seconded by Mr.
Moody. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Jason Sanchez, Community Recreation & Events Director, provided a staff report.
d)
Consideration of Bid #5-1 1-26 for an Agreement between the City of Cheyenne
and Miller and Sons Construction. Inc., for the Parsley Boulevard Greenway
Connectors project. (2021 Specific Purpose Tax Fund)
Mr. Wolfe moved to accept the bid in an amount not to exceed $228,970.80, seconded by Mr.
Moody. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Darci Hendon, THEENA Engineering, advised she was filling in for Jean Anderson-Shrednik,
Parks & Greenway Planner, and explained the proposed contract would connect greenway with an
existing sidewalk. Committee members Moody and White commented on the item.
OTHER ITEMS FOR TIlE AGENDA:
a)
Contract Modification #1 to Contract #7777 between the City of Cheyenne and the
Wyoming Department of Transportation for Federal Project B23 1031. Cheyenne
Streets, US3O, Dell Range Boulevard and Whitney Road Laramie County. (2023-
2026 Optional 1% Sales Tax Fund)
Mr Moody moved to approve in an amount not to exceed 5866.240.00. seconded by Mr. Wolfe.
Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Tom Cobb, City Engineer, provided a staff report.
b)
Cooperative Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and Laramie County for
Federal Project B23l031, Cheyenne Streets, US3O. Dell Range Boulevard and
Whitney Road Laramie County. (2023-2026 Optional 1% Sales Tax Fund)
Mr. Wolfe moved to approve in an amount not to exceed $2,523,500.00, seconded by Mr. Wolfe.
Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
